# Route map backdrop (D-043): a stylised painted Wanderkarte of the
# Salzkammergut, 320x180 exact. Meadow g with lighter y valley floors around
# lakes and rivers, G forests (g lit rim), painted peaks f/F with v foothills
# (the Schafberg with an h/i snow cap, the Zwoelferhorn south of St. Gilgen,
# Gaisberg, Osterhorn ridge, Katrin), lakes t with a T shore line and s
# glints (Wolfgangsee, Fuschlsee, Mondsee cut by the frame), Salzach, Ischl and
# Traun in T. Landmarks: the tiny Festung (i/m/w) on its hill at Salzburg,
# village houses (c/E/n) and churches (t spires) at the stations, the
# Falkenstein cliff (i/m/d) on the north shore, Bad Ischl's cluster, and a
# small torte on a plate under the Cafe Zauner dot. Wooden frame o/O/l.
# No text and no route line (the engine draws them); calm bottom band y >= 136.
# Station dots (route data starting layout): Salzburg 28,36; St. Gilgen
# 100,70; Brunnwinkl 124,58; Falkenstein 152,68; St. Wolfgang 180,84;
# Wolfgangsee 196,108; Strobl 232,118; Bad Ischl 276,98; Cafe Zauner 300,76.
# Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grid below is the
# source.
sprite = map_salzkammergut
size   = 320x180
origin = 0,0
anim   = idle frames=1
---
frame idle 0




















































































































































































